## 2026-10-21: two defects after the freeze; the freeze is reopened, once, with a validation gate
A fresh Fable instance checked K1 v2 (report kept with K1 in `tmp/replay/`, committed with it at reveal). K1 v2 reaches the violation in a faithful model of spec F (by a reply carrying a higher epoch moving the old coordinator, then a three-vote election under the larger configuration). It also found two defects in the frozen inputs:
1. **J1.2 as written is violated by the correct design.** Its first half ("every member's journal that has an entry at index i has that same entry there") fails whenever a lagging member holds a stale, uncommitted entry at an index committed elsewhere, which the design allows and the repaired design allows too. Every `--explore` would report it, and K1 could not tell repaired from faithful.
2. **`end: quiescent` cannot hold.** Coordinators heartbeat forever, and members outside the configuration (m5 before it is added; removed members after) time out and campaign forever, so a message is always in flight; every scenario would end `UNEXPLAINED bound`.
The freeze criterion says a defect found after the freeze is a residue. These two would make the registered measures unscoreable, no author has started, and no outcome exists, so **the freeze is reopened once**, for these two and their consequences only, disclosed here. Changes:
- Contract version 2: **J1.2 retired** (its id is never reused; any tag naming it is stale); **J1.4 (committed entries persist)**: if a coordinator commits the entry at index i in epoch e, then (a) every member elected coordinator in an epoch higher than e has that entry at index i when elected, and (b) no member that holds that entry at index i ever removes it from i. Every tag on J1.2 moves to J1.4 (scenarios, observe schema, briefs, K1).
- Scenario format: `end: quiescent` and the event end are replaced by `end: {settle: N}`: the run continues N events after the last step's action. FAIL if a clause is violated at any point; `UNEXPLAINED steps` if `bound` is reached before every step is taken; PASS otherwise. The contract has no liveness clause, so the end condition no longer asks for one.
- K1 becomes v3 (tags and end only); new hash logged with the change.
**The validation gate, new:** before the inputs freeze again, a reference model of spec F, written only to validate the inputs and never scored or compared with any author, runs every shared scenario and K1 in two variants: as specified, and with the gate (a change waits for a current-epoch commit). Required: both variants take every step of every shared scenario with no violation; the specified variant FAILs K1 on J1.4; the gated variant PASSes K1. The inputs freeze again only when all of that holds. Reason: three defects in a row (K1's triggers, J1.2, quiescence) were of the kind an execution finds at once and a reading does not, which is the replay's own thesis turned on its inputs. Written by a fresh Opus instance (the steward's family; it is not an arm), withheld with K1, committed at reveal. **Bound on the replay:** if the validation gate finds a further input defect that needs more than a mechanical fix, the steward will consider stopping the replay and recording why, rather than continue repairing.
Recorded as setup findings 11 and 12.

