   109	1. The validation gate passes; the inputs freeze (hashes regenerated); this file is reviewed once more by a fresh non-steward reader against the changes listed below.
   110	2. The hold-out author writes; hashes committed.
   111	3. Register: brief hashes and the gate's results table inserted; this file committed without the DRAFT line. The attribution script and the classification instructions are committed with it.
   112	4. Four history-free checkouts; `inputcheck-replay.sh` on each.
   113	5. Four authors start together.
   114	6. Classification (Grok, blind) and R4-before rating from each Choices and Concerns commit, committed before any steward run.
   115	7. The steward answers each author's declared limitations in the log.
   116	8. Steward runs of shared scenarios and mutations at each `first-version`; then the commit that reveals K1 and the hold-outs; then their runs.
