{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"1ae1aa8a-c979-4b7b-b194-caa214b86625","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Verdict: **(A)**\n\nBoth the model’s `PASS` and the implementation’s seed-2 `UNEXPLAINED steps` are consistent with the frozen inputs. Neither artifact violates the specification; the divergence comes from choices the inputs leave open across scheduling/sampling, selector resolution on self-removal, and optional administrative retry.\n\n---\n\n### Why the implementation’s behaviour on seed 2 is permitted by the specification\n\n1. **Initial coordinator selection is nondeterministic (`m3` may win the first election).**\n   - `replay/scenarios/S8.yaml` starts with `initial: [m1, m2, m3, m4]` and step 1:\n     \u003e `- {at: {event: Elected}, do: {remove: m3, at: coordinator}}`\n   - `replay/spec-D.md` (§3.4) leaves initial election timing randomized:\n     \u003e *\"To prevent split votes in the first place, election timeouts are chosen randomly from a fixed interval (e.g., 150–300 ms).\"*\n   - On seeds 1 and 3, a member other than `m3` wins the first election and `S8` reports `PASS`. On seed 2, `m3` wins the first election (`Elected` at `epoch: 1`, `member: \"m3\"`).\n\n2. **`m3` removes itself, replies `ok`, and is required to step down.**\n   - When `m3` is elected, step 1’s trigger `{event: Elected}` fires and resolves `coordinator` to `m3`.\n   - `replay/spec-D.md` (Source \u0026 Figure 4.1, `RemoveServer` step 4) requires a leader that removes itself to step down upon committing the removal and replying `OK`:\n     \u003e *\"...except that a coordinator that removes itself steps down after the change is committed, as Figure 4.1 (RemoveServer, step 4) says.\"*\n     \u003e *\"4. Reply OK and, if this server was removed, step down (§4.2.2)\"*\n\n3. **Step 2’s `coordinator` selector resolves to `m3` when `ChangeReplied(..., status: ok)` fires, and `m3` must reply `NOT_LEADER`.**\n   - `replay/scenarios/S8.yaml` step 2 is:\n     \u003e `- {at: {event: ChangeReplied, status: ok}, do: {add: m5, at: coordinator}}`\n   - `replay/scenario-format.md` specifies when selectors are resolved and when actions are taken:\n     \u003e *\"Once a trigger fires, the action is taken at some later point: the model explores every such point, the implementation samples one.\"*\n     \u003e *\"Three selectors may stand for a member name anywhere one is allowed, resolved when the step's trigger fires: `coordinator`, the member most recently `Elected`...\"*\n   - When `m3` emits `ChangeReplied` with `status: \"ok\"`, `m3` is still the member most recently `Elected`, so `coordinator` resolves to `m3`. Because `m3` has stepped down, `replay/spec-D.md` (Figure 4.1, `AddServer` step 1) requires:\n     \u003e *\"1. Reply NOT_LEADER if not leader (§6.2)\"*\n\n4. **Administrative retry after rejection is optional (`may`), so step 3’s trigger is never reached on seed 2.**\n   - `replay/failure-model.md` (Cell G1.4) permits—but does not require—retrying a rejected configuration change request at another member:\n     \u003e *\"G1.4 Administrative change. An add or remove request may arrive at any member at any moment. A request that the receiving member rejects or that times out may be retried at another member.\"*\n   - Without automatic retry of the rejected step-2 request `{add: m5, at: m3}`, no second `{event: ChangeReplied, status: ok}` is ever emitted, step 3 (`{at: {event: ChangeReplied, status: ok}, do: {add: m3, at: coordinator}}`) never triggers, and `replay/scenario-format.md` mandates `UNEXPLAINED steps`:\n     \u003e *\"If `bound` is reached before every step's action is taken, the outcome is `UNEXPLAINED steps` (the scenario never reached its point), never PASS.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Why the model’s `PASS` depends on choices the inputs leave open\n\n1. **Which member is elected first (and existential step-completion in the model vs. per-seed sampling in the implementation):**\n   - `replay/scenario-format.md` defines asymmetric pass/unexplained semantics for the two sides:\n     \u003e *\"Both sides compile a scenario: the model side into a TLC configuration that constrains the environment to the scenario's steps while exploring every interleaving it leaves open; the implementation side into fault injection and requests against a running system, sampled over seeds.\"*\n     \u003e *\"The model side explores every behaviour within its bounds that takes every step and at most N further events, with every prefix of such behaviours; it reports `UNEXPLAINED steps` if no behaviour within its bounds takes every step.\"*\n   - Because the inputs leave open which member wins the first election (and the model additionally bounds message delivery by rank order `m1 \u003c m2 \u003c m3 \u003c m4 \u003c m5`), any behaviour in which `m1`, `m2`, or `m4` is elected coordinator first does not trigger leader self-removal on `{remove: m3, at: coordinator}`, allowing all three steps to succeed with `status: ok`. Since such behaviours exist within the model's bounds (just as on implementation seeds 1 and 3), the model reports `PASS`.\n2. **Whether a rejected administrative request (`NOT_LEADER`) is retried at another member (`replay/failure-model.md` G1.4):**\n   - G1.4 states that a rejected request *\"may be retried at another member\"*, and `replay/scenario-format.md` leaves open whether a step `do: {add: m5, at: coordinator}` is sent once to the resolved member or retried after `NOT_LEADER`.\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"A\", \"choice_or_clause\": \"Initial leader election ordering / existential vs. sampled step completion (replay/scenario-format.md, spec-D.md §3.4) and whether a rejected administrative request is retried (replay/failure-model.md G1.4)\", \"reason\": \"In S8, step 1 removes m3 at coordinator. When a member other than m3 is elected first (as in the model's completing paths and implementation seeds 1 and 3), all three configuration changes succeed at that coordinator and yield PASS. On implementation seed 2, m3 is elected first (permitted by §3.4 randomized timeouts), removes itself, replies ok, and steps down as required by Figure 4.1 RemoveServer step 4. Under replay/scenario-format.md, step 2's trigger ({event: ChangeReplied, status: ok}) resolves coordinator at trigger time to the most recently Elected member (still m3), which must reply NOT_LEADER per Figure 4.1 AddServer step 1. Because G1.4 makes retrying a rejected request optional ('may be retried at another member') and the model reports UNEXPLAINED steps only if 'no behaviour within its bounds takes every step', both outcomes are permitted.\"}\n```\n","duration_seconds":53.621597699,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":25414,"output_tokens":4511,"thinking_tokens":2848,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":29925}}}
