{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9995595c-83b5-4476-93d5-6f0972c68668","status":"SUCCESS","response":"**Verdict: (A)** — the implementation's behaviour is permitted by the specification, and the model's `PASS` depends on choices that the inputs leave open.\n\n### Why\n\n1. **Why the implementation's `UNEXPLAINED steps` is permitted:**\n   - In `replay/scenarios/S6.yaml`, the cluster starts with `initial: [m1, m2, m3, m4]` (4 members, so a majority is 3).\n   - Step 2 (`at: {event: Committed}, do: {cut: [[m1, m3], [m1, m4], [m2, m3], [m2, m4]]}`) partitions the 4-member cluster 2–2 into `{m1, m2}` and `{m3, m4}`.\n   - Step 3 (`at: {event: Elected}, do: {heal: true}`) is only armed once step 2's `cut` action is taken:\n     \u003e \"step *i* is armed when step *i*−1's action is taken, and matches only events emitted after it was armed\" (`replay/scenario-format.md`)\n   - In `replay/spec-D.md`, a candidate requires a majority of the cluster (3 of 4 servers) to win an election:\n     \u003e \"A candidate wins an election if it receives votes from a majority of the servers in the full cluster for the same term.\" (`replay/spec-D.md`, §3.4; Figure 3.1)\n   - In the implementation's sampled execution, `cut` takes effect when no election is in flight across the cut, and while the 2–2 cut is active no candidate can collect 3 votes. Step 3 therefore never triggers before `bound: {events: 400}` is reached, which `replay/scenario-format.md` requires to be reported as `UNEXPLAINED steps`:\n     \u003e \"If `bound` is reached before every step's action is taken, the outcome is `UNEXPLAINED steps` (the scenario never reached its point), never PASS.\" (`replay/scenario-format.md`)\n   - Furthermore, `replay/contract.md` states:\n     \u003e \"There is no liveness clause in this contract.\"\n\n2. **What choices the inputs leave open that enable the model's `PASS`:**\n   - **Fate of in-flight messages across a link cut (`G1.3` / `G1.2`) and action/timeout timing after a trigger fires:**\n     - `replay/scenario-format.md` leaves open when an action is taken after its trigger fires (and states that the model explores every point while the implementation samples one):\n       \u003e \"Once a trigger fires, the action is taken at some later point: the model explores every such point, the implementation samples one.\" (`replay/scenario-format.md`)\n       \u003e \"The model side explores every behaviour within its bounds that takes every step and at most N further events, with every prefix of such behaviours; it reports `UNEXPLAINED steps` if no behaviour within its bounds takes every step.\" (`replay/scenario-format.md`)\n     - `replay/failure-model.md` defines `G1.2` and `G1.3` as:\n       \u003e \"- **G1.2 Message loss, delay, reordering and duplication.** Any message may be lost, delayed for any finite time, delivered out of order, or delivered more than once.\"\n       \u003e \"- **G1.3 Partition.** Links between members go down and come back, in either or both directions; while a link is down, messages sent over it are lost. (This is G1.2 applied systematically; it is a separate cell so that scenarios can name it.)\"\n     - This wording specifies that messages *sent while a link is down* are lost, leaving open whether messages *sent while the link was up* (before the `cut` action was taken) may remain queued in transit and be delivered after the link goes down.\n     - As the model author notes (`choice 12`), the model explores an interleaving where a new election starts after `Committed` (step 2's trigger) and sends `RequestVote` (and queues its reply) *before* step 2's `cut` action is taken, and then delivers that pre-cut message *after* the `cut` action is taken:\n       \u003e \"A new election can still finish after the 2–2 cut because a RequestVote that was sent while the link was up may be delivered afterwards (choice 12).\"\n       \u003e \"S6 still completes: the RequestVote reply queued while the link was up is delivered after the cut.\"\n\n{\"verdict\": \"A\", \"choice_or_clause\": \"Whether messages sent before a G1.3 link cut (while the link was up) may be delivered after the cut, combined with delayed execution of the cut action after its Committed trigger fires\", \"reason\": \"In S6, a 2-2 cut of the 4-member cluster [m1, m2, m3, m4] prevents any post-cut election from gathering a 3-vote majority unless an election message crosses the cut before the link goes down and is delivered after the cut. G1.3 states 'while a link is down, messages sent over it are lost' and scenario-format.md states 'Once a trigger fires, the action is taken at some later point: the model explores every such point, the implementation samples one.' The implementation permissibly takes the cut before any new election starts (and drops messages across the cut), hitting the 400-event bound (UNEXPLAINED steps), whereas the model reaches PASS by delaying the cut action until an election message is sent while the link is up and allowing that pre-cut message to be delivered after the cut (model choice 12).\"}\n","duration_seconds":46.133422888,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":25602,"output_tokens":4452,"thinking_tokens":3167,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":30054}}}

