    12	  # 4. m2, coordinator under C0 (no configuration entry in its journal), removes m4. C2 = {m1, m2, m3}, committed by m2 and m3; not sent to m4 by the specified design (a gated design must replicate its own epoch entry to m4 first, which is what blocks the trigger).
    13	  - {at: {event: Elected, member: m2}, do: {remove: m4, at: m2}}
    14	  # 5. Once m2 has committed, heal. m1 (C1, majority 3 of 5) can then be elected by m1, m4, m5, none of which holds C2: the coordinator lacks a committed entry (J1.5a), and its extend requests then remove it from m2 and m3 (J1.5b).
    15	  - {at: {event: Committed, member: m2}, do: {heal: true}}
    16	end: {settle: 100}
    17	bound: {events: 400}
     1	scenario: H1
     2	derives: [J1.5, G1.1, G1.4]
     3	initial: [m1, m2, m3, m4]
     4	steps:
     5	  # derives: H1 (J1.5, G1.1, G1.4). The coordinator starts an add and crashes with the new configuration entry in its own journal (and possibly m5's) but on no other member; the survivors elect under the old configuration and remove a member; the old coordinator restarts holding the dead configuration entry.
     6	  # Step 1: coordinator appends C1 = initial + m5 at index 1 (catch-up of m5 is immediate, initial configuration counts as committed).
     7	  - {at: {event: Elected}, do: {add: m5, at: coordinator}}
     8	  # Step 2: crash the coordinator at some point after C1 is in its journal; the interesting points are before C1 reaches any of the other original members.
     9	  - {at: {event: Appended, kind: config}, do: {crash: coordinator}}
    10	  # Step 3: a new coordinator is elected (under the initial configuration if C1 never reached it) and removes m4; C2 = initial - m4 at index 1 is committed by two of three.
    11	  - {at: {event: Elected}, do: {remove: m4, at: coordinator}}
    12	  # Step 4: once something is committed in the new epoch, restart the old coordinator; it comes back with C1 at index 1 and no knowledge of C2. m5 (if it holds C1) and the removed m4 are never told about C2.
    13	  - {at: {event: Committed}, do: {restart: crashed}}
