    87	
    88	<!-- derives: J1.1, J1.3, J1.5, G1.1, G1.2, G1.3, G1.4 -->
    89	
    90	1. The specification's justification for single-member changes concerns one
    91	   adjacent pair of configurations. It does not prove safety for a sequence of
    92	   configurations combined with early activation and stale coordinators. A
    93	   scenario could partition a coordinator, change membership elsewhere, then
    94	   let a stale member campaign against members with newer configurations.
