   800	24. **Bounds used for every scenario run.** A first attempt with `MaxTerm = 3`, `MaxMsgs = 12` and unordered delivery was still growing at depth 12: 2,856,132 distinct states and 2,071,413 queued. It would not finish under the 24G cap, so the cap was not raised. The runs below use the tighter bounds. S1–S8 each still have a completing path, and TLC exhausted each of those state spaces.
   801	
   802	    - `MaxTerm = 2`. S1, S2 and S6 need two elections. A split that would open a third term is not searched.
   803	    - `MaxLog = 3`. S8 appends three configuration entries and no shared scenario appends more.
   804	    - `MaxMsgs = 4`. One candidate's three RequestVote messages fit. A second candidate cannot queue its own three beside those, and a new leader cannot queue heartbeats until a slot is free.
   805	    - `MaxEvents` and `Settle` come from the scenario (400 and 100 on the shared files). A state at the cap is kept; the next event is not.
   806	    - `MaxDown = 20` in scenario mode so a cut of every directed pair is representable.
   807	    - At most one queued message on a directed pair.
   808	    - At most two servers have role candidate or leader. Two is enough for a second leader in one term, and for a stale leader beside one new candidate.
   809	    - `m5` stays a follower, including after it is added. It still votes and accepts AppendEntries.
   810	    - No server starts an election while any server has a configuration entry past its own `commitIndex`. S6 has no configuration entry, so the election across its cut still runs.
   811	    - The only delivery is the queued message with the lowest sender rank, then the lowest recipient rank. Ranks are `m1 < m2 < m3 < m4 < m5`.
   812	    - AppendEntries goes to the lowest-ranked peer that is behind on `matchIndex` and has none queued. When no peer is behind, the leader sends one heartbeat to the lowest peer, and only while it has no AppendEntries queued.
   813	    - A higher term resets `nextIndex` and `matchIndex`. Both are read only while the server is leader, and `BecomeLeader` overwrites them.
