     9	## Files
    10	- `tla/F.tla`: the model, in TLA+. It covers spec F, the SPEC and GATED variants, the scenario driver and the
    11	  checkers. This file is the readable statement of the model. `tla/F_v1_unreduced.tla` is the first version
    12	  (replies as separate messages); it was too slow to use and is kept only for the record.
    13	- `fexp/` (Rust, std only): the same transition system as `F.tla`, run as a parallel explicit-state DFS with
    14	  a shared lock-free 64-bit fingerprint table. It does about 1.5 to 2.5M states/s, where TLC on `F.tla`
    15	  managed about 15k states/s. Build it with `cargo build --release`.
    16	- `run.py`: the front end. It compiles a scenario YAML into either engine's input (`--engine fexp|tlc`),
    17	  runs it under the mandatory cap (`systemd-run --user --scope -q -p MemoryMax=24G -p MemorySwapMax=0`),
    18	  and reports `PASS`, `FAIL <clause>` with a trace, `UNEXPLAINED steps` or `UNEXPLAINED bound`.
    19	- `run_all.py`: runs every scenario against both variants with a ladder of bounds (see below) and prints the
    20	  table. Results are in `results/*.json`, logs in `logs/`, per-run inputs and outputs in `runs/`.
    21	- `explorer.py`, `pexplore.py`, `logs/probe_K1_SPEC.log`: the earlier uncapped attempt, left as found.
    22	  They were read, not used.
