    39	## The model
    40	It is spec F as written, with five members m1..m5. All five start with the scenario's initial configuration and
    41	an empty journal; non-members time out, vote and can be elected exactly like members, because the spec says
    42	requests are processed without consulting configuration. Durable state is epoch, votedFor and journal.
    43	A crash resets role, commitIndex, nextIndex/matchIndex, ballots and any pending change. Crash, restart, cut,
    44	drop, heal, add, remove and command happen only as scenario steps. Everything else is free nondeterminism:
    45	- a follower or candidate times out at any time; a coordinator never does;
    46	- any in-flight request is delivered at any later point, any number of times, or never;
    47	- the coordinator's local progress on a change happens at any later point.
    48	
    49	**Variants.**
    50	- SPEC is `Gated = FALSE`.
    51	- GATED is identical except for two things. On election a coordinator appends one `noop` command entry.
    52	  `Proceed` will not append a configuration entry until some entry at an index ≤ its commitIndex
    53	  carries its own epoch. Nothing else differs (`grep Gated tla/F.tla`).
